## How to vote in  
 2026 Elections

#### There are three ways for Suffolk County voters to cast a ballot in this year’s elections:

1.   ###### In Person during Early Voting at any one of the 28 Early Voting locations or on Primary or Election Day at your designated polling place. [To confirm your polling place location click HERE](https://voterlookup.elections.ny.gov/).

  
2.   ###### By Mail – By Early Mail ballot or by Absentee Ballot. [To Request a Ballot click HERE](https://elections.ny.gov/request-ballot).

  
3.   ###### Military and Oversees Voting - [For more information click HERE](https://elections.ny.gov/military-and-overseas-federal-voting).

  
4.   ###### Accessible Voting. Voters who are using the accessible ballot system can access printers in order to print their ballots at office supply stores and libraries, Voters with a disability will still be able to vote in-person using an accessible Ballot Marking Device (“BMD”), either during early voting or on Election Day. For more information click [HERE](https://elections.ny.gov/accessible-voting).

